    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §156.25, Pen L (as proposed in S.4516-C & A.7536-B)",
    "lawSection": "Penal Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7759\n\nSPONSOR: KAPLAN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the penal law, in relation to the crime of falsifying\nCOVID-19 vaccination records\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that makes changes to provisions of L.2021,\nc.784, to clarify certain provisions in the underlying chapter.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis bill clarifies that the unauthorized entering of computer material\nregarding COVID-19 vaccination status is considered computer tampering\nunder the penal law.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nNone.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation is a negotiated change to the underlying chapter.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 784 of the Laws of 2021. S.4516-C and\nA.7536-B passed the Senate and Assembly, respectively, in June 2021.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as a\nchapter of the laws of 2021 amending the penal law relating to making\nthe falsification of COVID-19 vaccination records a crime, as proposed\nin legislative bills numbers S. 4516-C and A.  7536-B, takes effect.\n",
